WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:38.866
[Music]

00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:43.966
[Narrator:] Rocky Mountain spotted fever,

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:48.099
a mysterious and usually fatal disease,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:57.033
was often called mountain fever, blue death, or black measles.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:05.060
It was much feared by early settlers of the Rocky 
Mountain region.

00:01:05.066 --> 00:01:11.266
The brown areas denote the counties from which 
one or more cases had been recognized

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:17.466
and reported as early as 1905.

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:32.099
It was especially dreaded in western Montana 
where four of every five victims died.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:47.766
Some people are convinced that the poison is in 
freshet water.

00:01:47.766 --> 00:01:59.332
Others say it is given off by decaying sawdust and 
pine needles.

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.299
A few Indians

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:13.066
believe...

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:19.199
it comes from the tick bite.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:29.966
Mr. Hawkins swears his boy got it

00:02:29.966 --> 00:02:41.799
from being near bare grass blossoms last June.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:51.333
It took a doctor almost three days to reach here.

00:02:51.333 --> 00:03:05.733
It was too late.

00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:13.166
Stimulated by Montana health authorities, 
scientists of national repute began experiments

00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:29.566
that brought exciting hope.

00:03:29.566 --> 00:03:35.299
Spotted fever transmitted by woodtick.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:41.400
Researchers had just completed an experiment 
that opens the field for an effective battle

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.933
against this terrible disease.

00:03:45.933 --> 00:03:56.733
Dr. H. T. Ricketts used the blood from a spotted- 
fever patient to infect experimental tick hosts.

00:03:56.733 --> 00:04:02.299
He permitted the suspected vector, dermacentor 
andersoni, to take a blood meal

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:12.533
from the infected guinea pigs.

00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:21.766
Now would the ticks from an infected host be 
infected, and would they transmit the infection

00:04:21.766 --> 00:04:32.532
to a normal host?

00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:49.733
The suspects did transmit spotted fever.

00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:56.599
These abandoned buildings immediately became 
laboratories.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:02.666
The federal aid and R. A. Cooley's Montana 
program were now joined

00:05:02.666 --> 00:05:11.232
against a dangerous disease that challenged a 
coordinated effort for four decades.

00:05:11.233 --> 00:05:19.366
The initial studies concentrated on the biology and 
possible control of the tick.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:33.933
Tick-flagging originated with these early workers 
and is still a most effective technique

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:41.599
for collecting the wood tick.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.566
Dermacentor andersoni was found to infest both 
small and large animals,

00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:52.166
and to have a two-year life cycle.

00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:57.832
Spring-hatched larva, the first of two immature 
stages,

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:03.699
were found drawing blood from small animals.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:09.300
These transform to nymphs, who go into 
hibernation from late summer

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:18.700
until the following spring.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:22.400
The second spring, a second stage.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:27.366
The nymphal ticks feed on small animals also.

00:06:27.366 --> 00:06:34.032
Infected larva or nymphs were found to infect their 
hosts whose blood then became infectious

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:40.233
for simultaneously feeding ticks.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:51.799
These will transform to adults by late summer, then 
hibernate.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:07:07.166
In the third spring, which completes the two-year 
cycle, the adults feed on large animals and man.

00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:19.732
Infected ticks, feeding on the small or large 
animals, do not cause obvious illness.

00:07:19.733 --> 00:07:27.033
The male has a mottled grey color pattern.

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:33.999
Before engorgement, this female was a dark 
reddish brown.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.833
They mate while feeding.

00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:43.366
Either sex may transmit the disease.

00:07:43.366 --> 00:07:51.999
Each female deposits 6,000 to 8,000 eggs on the 
ground.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:08:06.633
The larva from these may be infected and maintain 
their infection to adulthood.

00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:18.899
The disease is usually transmitted to man by adult 
ticks, of which about one percent are infected.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:33.400
A tick-host rodent-control program was initiated in 
a severely affected section of Western Montana

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:40.233
in 1911.

00:08:40.233 --> 00:08:56.599
Poisoned grain killed the rodents essential to the 
survival of the immature ticks.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:02.733
This program reduced the tick population and was 
continued for about twenty years

00:09:02.733 --> 00:09:07.466
until more effective disease control appeared.

00:09:07.466 --> 00:09:12.199
An extensive livestock-dipping program was also 
maintained.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.433
This was a direct attack on the adult ticks.

00:09:16.433 --> 00:09:25.066
These and minor control measures were effective 
but could only be afforded in limited areas.

00:09:25.066 --> 00:09:41.732
This was a typical tick control-era setting.

00:09:41.733 --> 00:09:48.699
It was in this laboratory that the first investigator 
became fatally infected.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:21.866
The bacterial-like infectious agent was found in all 
tissues of the tick.

00:10:21.866 --> 00:10:27.332
A stained preparation of infected tissue shows the 
red-stained agent,

00:10:27.333 --> 00:10:32.733
taxonomically designated rickettsia rickettsia.

00:10:32.733 --> 00:10:40.333
Virulent strains killed guinea pigs in 7 to 14 days.

00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:44.799
The scrotum and footpads became inflamed.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.833
These tissues finally died.

00:10:49.833 --> 00:11:10.766
An autopsy shows testes inflamed and adherent to 
body wall.

00:11:10.766 --> 00:11:20.299
Spleen enlarged.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:31.800
And lymph nodes enlarged.

00:11:38.066 --> 00:11:45.732
In 1921, investigators moved to a vacated country 
schoolhouse where another heartening

00:11:45.733 --> 00:11:53.933
breakthrough was made by Drs. Spencer and 
Parker.

00:11:53.933 --> 00:11:58.366
Spotted fever vaccine found.

00:11:58.366 --> 00:12:01.332
Spotted fever vaccine proven.

00:12:01.333 --> 00:12:10.233
Immunity through vaccination seems assured.

00:12:10.233 --> 00:12:26.366
Basically, the vaccine was made by grinding the 
highly-infected adult ticks in a phenol solution.

00:12:26.366 --> 00:12:31.166
Hand subrogation removed the coarse tissue.

00:12:31.166 --> 00:12:37.566
Clear vaccine contains the killed immunity-
producing rickettsii.

00:12:37.566 --> 00:12:52.699
A kitchen pressure cooker was used for a 
sterilizing autoclave.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:13:09.133
An alcohol lamp for flaming and a syringe for 
bottling the vaccine.

00:13:09.133 --> 00:13:13.933
Nineteen twenty-five, first year's output.

00:13:13.933 --> 00:13:16.366
Thousands exposed.

00:13:16.366 --> 00:13:18.832
Thirty-four vaccinated.

00:13:18.833 --> 00:13:25.899
Research expanded rapidly after 1928 when the 
state of Montana provided

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:36.633
the first safe modern facility.

00:13:36.633 --> 00:13:42.733
A tick-destroying parasite was now introduced to 
supplement the current rodent poisoning

00:13:42.733 --> 00:13:46.733
and stock-dipping control programs.

00:13:46.733 --> 00:13:57.933
This parasite, [?], deposits eggs in the nymphs by 
a stinging action.

00:13:57.933 --> 00:14:03.699
The maggot stage of this parasite kills the 
engorged nymphs by consuming their

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:12.433
host's internal organs.

00:14:12.433 --> 00:14:22.166
After a pupal stage, they emerge as adult 
parasites, ready to parasitize other nymphs.

00:14:22.166 --> 00:14:31.399
Millions of these parasites were reared for release 
near a small tick host lairs.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:37.533
Although parasites were successfully maintained in 
the laboratory, no parasitized nymphs

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:46.500
could be collected the following seasons.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.700
The startling recognition of spotted fever in some 
eastern states

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:12.920
suddenly made this a nationwide problem.

00:15:17.866 --> 00:15:26.760
Because of these pressures, the federal 
government purchased the Montana facility.

00:15:26.766 --> 00:15:34.232
A second unit was added in 1934.

00:15:34.233 --> 00:15:47.333
Millions of highly-infected ticks could now be 
reared annually for increased vaccine production.

00:15:47.333 --> 00:15:52.233
Mechanical grinders facilitated mass production.

00:15:52.233 --> 00:16:06.033
[Sound of machinery]

00:16:06.033 --> 00:16:18.066
A separatory funnel in a sterile room instead of the 
syringe for bottling.

00:16:18.066 --> 00:16:23.399
Potency and sterility testing could now be performed at the manufacturing laboratory

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:32.500
instead of at national headquarters.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:40.733
After 15 years of use, records demonstrated the protective value of the vaccine.

00:16:48.633 --> 00:16:57.166
In comparison with the production of only enough vaccine for 34 immunizations in 1925,

00:16:57.166 --> 00:17:05.099
there was now enough for use by physicians throughout the nation.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:11.400
By 1940, additional facilities made it possible to accommodate more scientists

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:19.266
and broaden the research to include other diseases in nature communicable to man.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:18:01.180
The diseases studied by then are noted in the top line of each experimental animal card.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:19.233
Another milestone in the expanding struggle against spotted fever was Dr. H. R. Cox's first time

00:18:19.233 --> 00:18:26.733
culturing a rickettsii in embryonic egg tissue.

00:18:26.733 --> 00:18:34.633
Rickettsia rickettsii could now be produced more 
efficiently, and it eliminated the stray tick hazard.

00:18:34.633 --> 00:18:40.066
Eggs containing eight-day embryos were 
inoculated with spotted fever,

00:18:40.066 --> 00:18:46.732
and incubated further.

00:18:46.733 --> 00:19:11.799
Highly-infected yolk sacs were harvested from 
mechanically-opened eggs.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:15.200
Yolk sacs were blended, and a phenol formula solution was added

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:24.466
to kill and preserve the rickettsii.

00:19:24.466 --> 00:19:38.560
And fats were extracted with ether.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:20:00.400
By now, field information on ticks from across the nation was needed to complete epidemiological data

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.466
on the various tick-borne diseases.

00:20:04.466 --> 00:20:10.500
The entomologists found many species, some in the ground...

00:20:16.566 --> 00:20:23.360
some on trees and in the jungle, as well as in the desert.

00:20:23.366 --> 00:20:30.266
Information on their taxonomic determination, disease transmission potential,

00:20:30.266 --> 00:20:45.699
and distribution were essential.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:51.600
Three species were found to infect man: the wood tick,

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:59.600
[Map of US shown]

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.033
the dog tick,

00:21:08.533 --> 00:21:14.099
[Map of US shown]

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:26.100
and the Lone Star tick.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:42.240
Spotted fever is still an ever-present danger to those who live in or visit wood tick-infested areas.

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:59.100
These are typical exposures to the wood tick.

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:04.633
Exposure to the dog tick could, of course, take 
place in the home.

00:22:04.633 --> 00:22:12.833
The time of greatest exposure to the tick is in the 
spring and early summer.

00:22:12.833 --> 00:22:20.766
That this tick is infected.

00:22:20.766 --> 00:22:26.532
Contrary to common belief, the tick's mouth parts seldom remain imbedded in the skin

00:22:26.533 --> 00:22:34.033
after the specimen's removal.

00:22:34.033 --> 00:22:45.799
Influenza-like symptoms appear about one week 
after the bite of an infected tick.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:49.200
Serological diagnosis for tick-borne diseases was a routine service

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:54.466
at the Rocky Mountain Laboratory.

00:22:54.466 --> 00:23:03.199
Physicians also depended upon its scientists for 
the most recent information on these diseases.

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:14.933
One such test was the Weil-Felix for spotted fever.

00:23:14.933 --> 00:23:19.033
Treatment was usually symptomatic.

00:23:19.033 --> 00:23:26.733
In other words, major discomforts could be 
alleviated, but the disease would run its course.

00:23:26.733 --> 00:23:40.799
A rash usually appears on the wrists and ankles 
sometime during the first week.

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:45.433
It soon covers the entire body.

00:23:45.433 --> 00:23:53.433
In severe cases, it later becomes confluent.

00:23:53.433 --> 00:24:01.933
When the illness is fatal, death usually occurs during the second week of illness.

00:24:01.933 --> 00:24:05.799
Non-fatal cases are bedfast two to three weeks.

00:24:22.666 --> 00:24:29.599
Vaccination is advisable each spring for those 
extensively exposed to ticks.

00:24:29.600 --> 00:24:41.766
In high-incident areas, it was made available 
through free vaccination clinics.

00:24:41.766 --> 00:24:48.240
Avoid the carriers. They wait on low vegetation.

00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:58.420
Do not wear clothing that is open at the bottom.

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:13.300
They are attracted by the body odor under the 
garment.

00:25:13.300 --> 00:25:20.060
To avoid bites, each garment should fit over the 
one above.

00:25:23.700 --> 00:25:29.933
Even so, the entire body and both sides of the 
clothing should be thoroughly examined

00:25:29.940 --> 00:25:33.180
before retiring.

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:45.266
Once on the neck, it is usually felt before it 
attaches.

00:25:45.266 --> 00:25:51.432
The long-sought wonder cure came in the late 1940s with the commercial introduction

00:25:51.433 --> 00:26:00.099
of certain antibiotics.

00:26:00.100 --> 00:26:05.666
They have greatly reduced the death rate and the fear of this once dread malady

00:26:05.666 --> 00:26:11.799
has essentially disappeared.

00:26:19.066 --> 00:26:23.432
Spotted fever fought back for half a century,

00:26:23.433 --> 00:26:32.766
from Ricketts' tick transmission experiment to antibiotics, and took the lives of five researchers.

00:26:32.766 --> 00:26:37.932
McClintock.

00:26:37.933 --> 00:26:41.133
McCray.

00:26:41.133 --> 00:26:46.833
Cowan.

00:26:46.840 --> 00:26:51.900
Kerlee.

00:26:59.140 --> 00:27:04.400
To the memory of our fellow laboratory workers who, while engaged in the study

00:27:04.400 --> 00:27:14.733
of Rocky Mountain Spotted Fever, have contracted the disease and died.

00:27:14.733 --> 00:27:22.399
As after the victory over other historically notorious infectious diseases,

00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:26.033
these costs are now being repaid.

00:27:26.033 --> 00:27:33.099
The developments and knowledge gained have made fatal spotted fever cases the exception

00:27:33.100 --> 00:27:37.600
and eliminated the universal fear.

00:27:37.600 --> 00:27:42.466
It is no longer a disease of mystery.

00:27:42.466 --> 00:28:10.400
[Music]

